<title>UK: BOE forecasts 900 mln stg shortage, offers help.</title>
<headline>BOE forecasts 900 mln stg shortage, offers help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England offered an early round of assistance to the UK money market after forecasting a liquidity shortage of around 900 million stg.</p>
<p>The Bank offered a fixed round of operations comprising repos to April 22 and 23 and outright bills maturing on or before April 23.</p>
